text:
lee: Noticing a tail latency uptick for short streaming requests after yesterday's kernel routing tweak. p99 up ~18% on hosts.

maya: thanks for flagging. Any traces or quick diffs?

lee: Attached trace points to many small writev/syscall bursts inside the stream emitter. Flame shows emitter::emit -> socket::writev -> grpc_layer::send. Also increased memcpy in tokenizer output path.

drew: I also observed an increase in kvcache churn during the same window. Might be related: smaller fragments cause more frequent kvcache lookups/evictions because request bytes are split differently.

oscar: did the kernel router change change frame aggregation behavior?

lee: It did. The router now prefers a low-latency kernel for sequences < 80 tokens, but that kernel path disabled the coalesce_hint which used to let the host combine tiny frames. Result: immediate flushes.

maya: can we re-enable coalescing at the host edge as a bandaid?

lee: Tried a local emitter shim to batch tiny fragments prior to writev. Quick patch reduced syscall counts and helped p99 significantly. Diff I used (simplified):
```
--- a/stream/emitter.cc
+++ b/stream/emitter.cc
@@ -88,7 +88,17 @@
-  socket.writev(frags);
+  // batch tiny fragments to avoid syscall and gRPC-layer churn
+  FragmentBatch batch;
+  for (auto &f : frags) {
+    if (f.len < 256 && batch.total_len < 1024) {
+      batch.append(f);
+      continue;
+    }
+    if (!batch.empty()) { socket.writev(batch.to_iovec()); batch.clear(); }
+    socket.writev(f.to_iovec());
+  }
+  if (!batch.empty()) socket.writev(batch.to_iovec());
```

drew: results?

lee: Canary (5% traffic, 25m): p50 115ms -> 112ms, p95 260ms -> 245ms, p99 460ms -> 360ms. KV evictions down ~14%. Sys CPU down ~9%. perf-bot logged metrics.

perf-bot: canary/5%/25m: p50 115ms->112ms, p95 260ms->245ms, p99 460ms->360ms; kvcache.evictions -14%; syscall_count per request -40%.

oscar: good signal. We should do two things: 1) revert the router change that dropped coalesce_hint until we have a selector test, and 2) land the host-side coalesce as a hardening change. Also add a microbench that exercises short-stream writev counts.

maya: agree. opened RNDF-1234 to preserve coalesce_hint in selector and add microbench + CI assertion.

lee: created hotfix PR for emitter coalesce + test coverage. Planning rollback window for router patch tomorrow 10:00 PST if no objections.

deploy-bot: deploy/212 started (canary 5%) with emitter-coalesce hotfix.

oscar: also note some HTTP/1.1 clients triggered header flushes when frames were tiny; coalescing reduced header churn in logs. Please include a short note in the PR about HTTP behavior so support knows.

drew: will follow-up with flamegraphs and the small-stream microbench script. Also adding telemetry: writev_calls_per_request and small_frag_ratio so we can alert if this regresses.

lee: thanks all. If canary numbers hold at 12h, we can promote. I'll post final flamegraphs and the microbench link. :thumbsup:
